/* Baustein aa: Adjective or adverb. Automatisch erzeugt, nicht von Hand ändern. */
GT_UNIT({"id":"aa","title":"Adjective or adverb","ruleTitle":"Adjective or adverb","date":"2026-10-06","sets":{"b":[{"n":"Adjective or adverb?","p":["b1"]},{"n":"Special adverbs","p":["b2"]}],"k":[{"n":"-er or more?","p":["k1"]},{"n":"better, worse and adverbs","p":["k2"]}],"p":[{"n":"look, feel, taste, sound","p":["p1"]},{"n":"hard or hardly?","p":["p2"]}]},"tags":{"AD":"Adjektiv oder Adverb (Nomen oder Verb)","LY":"Bildung der Adverbien: -ly, well, fast, hard","CA":"Steigerung der Adjektive (-er / -est, more / most, than)","IR":"Unregelmäßige Steigerung (better, worse, further)","CV":"Steigerung der Adverbien (more carefully, faster)","LV":"Adjektiv nach look, feel, taste, smell, sound, seem","AV":"Adverb vor Adjektiv (really tired)","HL":"hard oder hardly, late oder lately"},"coach":"Before you choose, look at the word it describes. If it describes a noun, you need an adjective. If it describes a verb, you need an adverb.","quips":{"AD":["An adjective tells you what somebody is like, and an adverb tells you how they do something.","Look at the word it describes. A noun wants an adjective, and a verb wants an adverb."],"LY":["Good is the adjective, and well is its adverb. You play well, sing well and sleep well.","Fast, hard and late are adverbs already, so they don't take -ly."],"CA":["Short adjectives take -er and -est, and long ones take more and most. It is never both.","After a comparative English says than. As only appears in pairs: as tall as."],"IR":["Good, better, best and bad, worse, worst are the ones you simply have to know."],"CV":["An adverb with -ly is always long, so it takes more: more carefully."],"LV":["After look, feel, taste, smell and sound you describe the thing itself, so you need an adjective.","Somebody painted my nose green last week. I looked ridiculous, and that takes an adjective."],"AV":["The word in front of an adjective says how much, and that is a job for an adverb."],"HL":["Hardly means almost not. Somebody who hardly works is not working hard at all.","Late means not on time, and lately means in the last few weeks."]},"tasks":{"b1":"Adjective or adverb?","b2":"Adjective or adverb?","bc":"Adjective or adverb?","k1":"Use the comparative or the superlative.","k2":"Use the comparative or the superlative.","kc":"Use the comparative or the superlative.","p1":"Adjective or adverb?","p2":"With -ly or without?","pc":"With -ly or without?"},"card":{"top":["Which word does it describe?","A noun → adjective. A verb → adverb."],"lines":[{"s":"b1","r":"A noun takes an adjective. A verb takes an adverb.","e":"He is a {careful} <<driver>>. // He <<drives>> {carefully}.","n":"Adverb = adjective + -ly: slow → slowly · quiet → quietly // After be → adjective: The <<test>> was {easy}."},{"s":"b2","r":"good → well · fast, hard and late stay the same","e":"She is a {good} <<singer>>. She <<sings>> {well}. // He is a {fast} <<runner>>. He <<runs>> {fast}.","n":"Spelling: happy → happily · terrible → terribly · fantastic → fantastically"},{"s":"k1","r":"Short adjectives: -er, -est. Long adjectives: more, most.","e":"I am {taller} [than] my dad. · I am the {tallest} in my family. // Maths is {more difficult} [than] art. · It is the {most difficult} subject.","n":"Short = one syllable, or two with -y: big → bigger · nice → nicer · happy → happier // Equal: [as] {tall} [as] my dad · German trap „größer als“ → taller [than] ~as~"},{"s":"k2","r":"good → better → best · bad → worse → worst","e":"Your idea is {better} [than] mine. // This is the {worst} pizza in town.","n":"Also: far → further → furthest"},{"s":"k2","r":"Adverbs: -ly → more · no -ly → -er","e":"Can you <<drive>> {more carefully}? // She <<runs>> {faster} [than] me.","n":"well → better · badly → worse"},{"s":"p1","r":"After look, feel, taste, smell, sound, seem → adjective","e":"<<You>> [look] {tired}. · It [tastes] {good}. // She <<looked>> at me {angrily}. ^an action^","n":"German trap: ~It tastes well.~"},{"s":"p1","r":"How cold? → adverb + adjective","e":"It was {terribly} <<cold>>. // She [looks] {really} <<happy>>."},{"s":"p2","r":"hardly = almost not · lately = in the last few weeks","e":"She <<works>> {hard}. · She {hardly} <<works>>. ^almost not^ // The bus <<came>> {late}. · I have not <<seen>> him {lately}.","n":"Hard and late are adverbs already. With -ly they become new words."}],"key":"<<blue>> the word it describes · {red} adjective or adverb · [yellow] signal word"},"lessons":{"b1":{"t":"Adjective or adverb?","s":[{"b":"He is a {careful} <<driver>>.","t":"Careful is an adjective. It tells you what somebody or something is like, and here it describes a noun: the driver."},{"b":"He is a {careful} <<driver>>. // He <<drives>> {carefully}.","t":"Carefully is an adverb. It tells you how somebody does something, so it describes the verb: drives."},{"b":"{slow} → {slowly} · {quiet} → {quietly} · {careful} → {carefully}","t":"Most adverbs are easy to build. You take the adjective and add -ly."},{"b":"Er ist vorsichtig. Er fährt vorsichtig. // He is {careful}. He <<drives>> {carefully}.","t":"German uses the same word both times, and that is why this goes wrong so often. English makes you choose.","m":"dry"},{"b":"The <<test>> was {easy}. · <<She>> is {nervous}.","t":"One more thing. After be, so after am, is, are, was and were, you need an adjective. It describes the person or the thing, not an action."},{"b":"a noun → {adjective} // a verb → {adverb}","t":"So look at the word it describes. A noun takes an adjective, and a verb takes an adverb."}],"k":[[{"b":"She answered the question ___.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["politely","polite","politeness"],"c":0,"r":"Yes. Answered is a verb, so it takes an adverb.","w":"No. Answered is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: She answered the question politely."},{"b":"That was a ___ mistake.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["stupidly","stupid","stupidity"],"c":1,"r":"Right. Mistake is a noun, so it takes an adjective.","w":"No. Mistake is a noun, and a noun takes an adjective: That was a stupid mistake."}],[{"b":"They <<waited>> {nervously}.","t":"Why \"nervously\" and not \"nervous\"?","o":["Because it describes the verb \"waited\".","Because they were late.","Because nervous is a long word."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. It says how they waited, so it is an adverb.","w":"No. It describes the verb \"waited\". It says how they did it, and that takes an adverb."},{"b":"The <<answer>> was {wrong}.","t":"Why \"wrong\" and not \"wrongly\"?","o":["Because the answer was short.","Because it comes after \"was\" and describes the answer.","Because wrong has no adverb."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. After be you need an adjective.","w":"No. It comes after \"was\" and describes a noun, the answer. That takes an adjective."}]]},"b2":{"t":"Special adverbs","s":[{"b":"She is a {good} <<singer>>. She <<sings>> {well}.","t":"A few adverbs do not follow the -ly rule. The most important one is well. Good is the adjective, and well is its adverb."},{"b":"~She sings good.~ She <<sings>> {well}.","t":"\"She sings good\" is the classic slip. Sings is a verb, so it takes the adverb, and the adverb is well.","m":"dry"},{"b":"He is a {fast} <<runner>>. He <<runs>> {fast}.","t":"Fast does not change at all. It is an adjective and an adverb, and there is no \"fastly\"."},{"b":"{fast} → {fast} · {hard} → {hard} · {late} → {late}","t":"Hard and late work in the same way. You work hard, and the bus arrives late."},{"b":"happy → {happily} · terrible → {terribly} · fantastic → {fantastically}","t":"And three endings change the spelling. A -y turns into -ily, -le turns into -ly, and -ic takes -ally."}],"k":[[{"b":"You dance really ___.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["good","well","goodly"],"c":1,"r":"Yes. Well is the adverb of good.","w":"No. Dance is a verb, so you need the adverb of good: You dance really well."},{"b":"This car goes really ___.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["fast","fastly","more fast"],"c":0,"r":"Right. Fast stays the same.","w":"No. Fast is an adjective and an adverb, and there is no \"fastly\": This car goes really fast."}],[{"b":"They <<won>> {easily}.","t":"Why \"easily\" and not \"easyly\"?","o":["Because a -y at the end turns into -ily.","Because easy is a short word.","Because won is an irregular verb."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Easy, easily. Happy, happily.","w":"No. When the adjective ends in -y, the adverb ends in -ily: easy, easily."},{"b":"We <<trained>> {hard}.","t":"Why \"hard\" and not \"hardly\"?","o":["Because training is tiring.","Because hard is a short word.","Because hard stays the same as an adverb."],"c":2,"r":"Exactly. Hard, fast and late do not take -ly.","w":"No. Hard stays the same as an adverb. Hardly is a different word with a different meaning."}]]},"k1":{"t":"Comparing things","s":[{"b":"I am {tall}. My dad is {tall} too.","t":"When you compare two things, the adjective changes. English has two ways to do that, and the length of the adjective decides."},{"b":"I am {taller} [than] my dad. · I am the {tallest} in my family.","t":"Short adjectives take -er and -est. Taller compares two people, and the tallest is number one in a group. After the -er form you say than."},{"b":"big → {bigger} · nice → {nicer} · happy → {happier}","t":"Short means one syllable, or two syllables with -y at the end. Watch the spelling: big doubles the g, and the -y turns into -i."},{"b":"Maths is {more difficult} [than] art. · It is the {most difficult} subject.","t":"Long adjectives do not change. They take more and most in front: more difficult, the most difficult."},{"b":"~more tall~ {taller} // ~difficulter~ {more difficult}","t":"You never use both. It is either -er or more, and the length of the adjective tells you which.","m":"dry"},{"b":"größer als → {taller} [than] ~as~ // so groß wie → [as] {tall} [as] my dad","t":"Here is the German trap. \"Als\" is than, not as. You only need as when two things are equal: as tall as. The adjective stays in its base form there."}],"k":[[{"b":"This bag is ___ than mine.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["heavier","more heavy","heavyer"],"c":0,"r":"Yes. Heavy ends in -y, so it is heavier.","w":"No. Heavy has two syllables and ends in -y, so it takes -er, and the -y turns into -i: heavier."},{"b":"That was the ___ game of the season.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["excitingest","most exciting","more exciting"],"c":1,"r":"Right. A long adjective takes most.","w":"No. Exciting is a long adjective, and \"the … of the season\" needs the superlative: the most exciting game."}],[{"b":"The film is {more interesting} [than] the book.","t":"Why \"more interesting\" and not \"interestinger\"?","o":["Because interesting is a long adjective.","Because the film is new.","Because than comes after it."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Long adjectives take more and most.","w":"No. Interesting is a long adjective, and long adjectives take more and most."},{"b":"My room is {smaller} [than] yours.","t":"Why \"smaller\" and not \"more small\"?","o":["Because the room is tiny.","Because small is a short adjective.","Because yours comes after it."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. Short adjectives take -er and -est.","w":"No. Small has one syllable, and short adjectives take -er and -est."}]]},"k2":{"t":"Irregular forms and adverbs","s":[{"b":"good → {better} → {best} // bad → {worse} → {worst}","t":"Two adjectives go their own way, and they are the two you need most. Good, better, best. Bad, worse, worst."},{"b":"Your idea is {better} [than] mine. // This is the {worst} pizza in town.","t":"There is no \"gooder\" and no \"more bad\". Far is the third one: far, further, furthest."},{"b":"He <<drives>> {carefully}.","t":"Adverbs can be compared too, and you already know how to build them."},{"b":"Can you <<drive>> {more carefully}?","t":"An adverb with -ly is always long, so it takes more and most: more carefully, more politely, more clearly."},{"b":"She <<runs>> {faster} [than] me. // She <<sings>> {better} [than] me.","t":"The adverbs without -ly take -er and -est: faster, harder, later. Well and badly share the forms of good and bad: well, better, best and badly, worse, worst."},{"b":"adjective: {careful} → {more careful} // adverb: {carefully} → {more carefully}","t":"So first decide whether you need an adjective or an adverb, and then compare it."}],"k":[[{"b":"My handwriting is ___ than yours.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["badder","worse","more bad"],"c":1,"r":"Yes. Bad, worse, worst.","w":"No. Bad is irregular: bad, worse, worst. My handwriting is worse than yours."},{"b":"This is the ___ burger I have ever had.","t":"Which form fits?","o":["best","goodest","most good"],"c":0,"r":"Right. Good, better, best.","w":"No. Good is irregular: good, better, best. This is the best burger I have ever had."}],[{"b":"Please <<speak>> {more clearly}.","t":"Why \"more clearly\" and not \"clearlier\"?","o":["Because adverbs with -ly take more.","Because clear is a short word.","Because please comes first."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. An adverb with -ly takes more and most.","w":"No. Clearly is an adverb with -ly, and those take more and most."},{"b":"He <<works>> {harder} [than] me.","t":"Why \"harder\" and not \"more hardly\"?","o":["Because he is lazy.","Because hard has no -ly, so it takes -er.","Because than comes after it."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. Hard, harder. Fast, faster.","w":"No. The adverb is hard, without -ly, and adverbs without -ly take -er: harder."}]]},"p1":{"t":"What does it describe?","s":[{"b":"He <<drives>> {carefully}.","t":"You know the rule: a verb takes an adverb. A few verbs are different, because they do not describe an action at all."},{"b":"<<You>> [look] {tired}. · It [tastes] {good}.","t":"Look and taste do not say what somebody does here. They say what somebody or something is like, just as be does. So the word after them describes the noun, and it is an adjective."},{"b":"[look] · [feel] · [taste] · [smell] · [sound] · [seem]","t":"These six work in that way. German says \"Das schmeckt gut\", and the trap is to translate it with well. It is \"It tastes good\", with an adjective."},{"b":"<<You>> [look] {tired}. · It [tastes] {good}. // She <<looked>> at me {angrily}. ^an action^","t":"Be careful with look. When somebody looks at something, that is an action, and an action takes an adverb again.","m":"dry"},{"b":"It was {terribly} <<cold>>.","t":"Now the second point. Sometimes a word does not describe a noun or a verb, but an adjective. Terribly tells you how cold it was, and that is a job for an adverb."},{"b":"It was {terribly} <<cold>>. // She [looks] {really} <<happy>>.","t":"Both rules can meet in one sentence. Happy is an adjective, because it comes after looks. Really is an adverb, because it describes happy."}],"k":[[{"b":"This song sounds ___.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["familiar","familiarly","more familiarly"],"c":0,"r":"Yes. After sound you need an adjective.","w":"No. Sounds says what the song is like, so you need an adjective: This song sounds familiar."},{"b":"The exam was ___ difficult.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["extreme","extremely","extremer"],"c":1,"r":"Right. Extremely describes the adjective difficult.","w":"No. Difficult is an adjective, and the word that describes an adjective is an adverb: extremely difficult."}],[{"b":"The <<milk>> [smells] {strange}.","t":"Why \"strange\" and not \"strangely\"?","o":["Because it says what the milk is like.","Because milk is a short word.","Because smells ends in -s."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. After smell you describe the thing, so you need an adjective.","w":"No. Smells does not describe an action here. It says what the milk is like, and that takes an adjective."},{"b":"He <<looked>> at the map {carefully}.","t":"Why \"carefully\" and not \"careful\"?","o":["Because the map was old.","Because looking at something is an action.","Because careful has no adverb."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. An action takes an adverb.","w":"No. He looked at the map, and that is an action. An action takes an adverb."}]]},"p2":{"t":"hard or hardly, late or lately","s":[{"b":"We <<trained>> {hard}. · The match <<started>> {late}.","t":"You know that hard and late are adverbs already and take no -ly. But hardly and lately exist too. They are different words with different meanings."},{"b":"She <<works>> {hard}. · She {hardly} <<works>>. ^almost not^","t":"Hard means with a lot of effort. Hardly means almost not. So the second sentence says the opposite of the first one."},{"b":"I can {hardly} <<wait>>. · We have {hardly} any milk.","t":"Hardly comes before the verb, or after can and could. You also meet it in \"hardly any\" and \"hardly ever\". German says \"kaum\"."},{"b":"The bus <<came>> {late}. · I have not <<seen>> him {lately}.","t":"Late means not on time. Lately means in the last few weeks, and it often comes with the present perfect."},{"b":"{hard} = with effort · {hardly} = almost not // {late} = not on time · {lately} = in the last few weeks","t":"So with these two, -ly does not turn an adjective into an adverb. It makes a new word.","m":"dry"}],"k":[[{"b":"He ___ ate anything at lunch.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["hard","hardly","harder"],"c":1,"r":"Yes. Hardly means almost not.","w":"No. He ate almost nothing, and that is hardly: He hardly ate anything at lunch."},{"b":"Sorry, we arrived ___.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["late","lately","latest"],"c":0,"r":"Right. Late means not on time.","w":"No. Not on time is late. Lately means in the last few weeks: Sorry, we arrived late."}],[{"b":"I have not <<played>> much {lately}.","t":"What does \"lately\" tell you?","o":["That it is about the last few weeks.","That the speaker was not on time.","That the speaker plays badly."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Lately means in the last few weeks.","w":"No. Lately has nothing to do with being on time. It means in the last few weeks."},{"b":"He {hardly} <<trains>>.","t":"What does this sentence tell you?","o":["He trains a lot.","He almost never trains.","He trains in the evening."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. Hardly means almost not.","w":"No. Hardly means almost not, so he almost never trains."}]]}},"items":[{"i":"e-01","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"My brother drives ___ (careful), but he parks like a pirate.","f":"","g":"","a":[["carefully"]],"h":["carefully"]},{"i":"e-02","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"Be ___ (quiet)! The baby has just fallen asleep.","f":"","g":"","a":[["quiet"]],"h":["quiet"]},{"i":"e-03","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"She plays the drums really ___ (good). The neighbours disagree.","f":"","g":"","a":[["well"]],"h":["well"]},{"i":"e-04","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"You solved that ___ (easy). Are you secretly a genius?","f":"","g":"","a":[["easily"]],"h":["easily"]},{"i":"e-05","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"My little sister is already ___ (tall) than me. It is embarrassing.","f":"","g":"","a":[["taller"]],"h":["taller"]},{"i":"e-06","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"That was the ___ (bad) film I have ever seen. I want my two hours back.","f":"","g":"","a":[["worst"]],"h":["worst"]},{"i":"e-07","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"The second season is ___ (exciting) than the first one.","f":"","g":"","a":[["more exciting"]],"h":["more exciting"]},{"i":"e-08","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"Next time, read the question ___ (careful) than you did today.","f":"","g":"","a":[["more carefully"]],"h":["more carefully"]},{"i":"e-09","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"This soup tastes ___ (strange). What did you put in it?","f":"","g":"","a":[["strange"]],"h":["strange"]},{"i":"e-10","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"I ___ (hard) slept last night. The neighbours had a party.","f":"","g":"","a":[["hardly"]],"h":["hardly"]},{"i":"e-11","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"It is ___ (extreme) hot in here. Can somebody open a window?","f":"","g":"","a":[["extremely"]],"h":["extremely"]},{"i":"e-12","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"Have you seen Jonas ___ (late)? He never answers my messages.","f":"","g":"","a":[["lately"]],"h":["lately"]},{"i":"b1-01","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"My brother packed his bag ___ and still forgot his shoes.","f":"\"Packed\" is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: carefully.","g":"AD","c":"carefully","w":["careful","more careful"]},{"i":"b1-02","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"That was a ___ answer. Did you practise it in front of the mirror?","f":"\"Answer\" is a noun, and a noun takes an adjective: a perfect answer.","g":"AD","c":"perfect","w":["perfectly","perfection"]},{"i":"b1-03","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"Our goalkeeper is ___, but today he played ___.","f":"After \"is\" you need an adjective: brilliant. \"Played\" is a verb and takes an adverb: terribly.","g":"AD","c":"brilliant … terribly","w":["brilliantly … terrible","brilliant … terrible"]},{"i":"b1-04","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"She smiled ___ and said nothing. That is never a good sign.","f":"\"Smiled\" is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: politely.","g":"AD","c":"politely","w":["polite","politeness"]},{"i":"b1-05","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"You are talking about your coach. Which sentence is correct?","f":"\"Explained\" is a verb, so you need the adverb: clearly.","g":"AD","c":"He explained the rules clearly.","w":["He explained the rules clear.","He clear explained the rules."]},{"i":"b1-06","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"The exam was ___. I finished after twenty minutes and drew a cat on the last page.","f":"After \"was\" you need an adjective. It describes the exam: short.","g":"AD","c":"short","w":["shortly","shortness"]},{"i":"b1-07","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"Maya is a ___ person, but she drives ___.","f":"\"Person\" is a noun: calm. \"Drives\" is a verb: dangerously.","g":"AD","c":"calm … dangerously","w":["calmly … dangerous","calm … dangerous"]},{"i":"b1-08","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"The dog sat next to my sandwich and waited ___.","f":"\"Waited\" is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: patiently.","g":"AD","c":"patiently","w":["patient","patience"]},{"i":"b1-09","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence describes how somebody does something?","f":"\"Honestly\" is an adverb. It tells you how she answers. \"Honest\" tells you what she is like.","g":"AD","c":"She answers honestly.","w":["She is honest."]},{"i":"b1-10","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"My sister reads my messages ___ (secret). I have changed my password three times.","f":"\"Reads\" is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: secretly.","g":"AD","a":[["secretly"]],"h":["secretly"]},{"i":"b1-11","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"I was ___ (nervous) before the presentation, so I forgot my own name.","f":"After \"was\" you need an adjective. It describes \"I\": nervous.","g":"AD","a":[["nervous"]],"h":["nervous"]},{"i":"b1-12","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"He answered every question ___ (correct) and then forgot to write his name on the paper.","f":"\"Answered\" is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: correctly.","g":"AD","a":[["correctly"]],"h":["correctly"]},{"i":"b1-13","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"Jonas is a ___ (serious) gamer. He has a spreadsheet for his high scores.","f":"\"Gamer\" is a noun, and a noun takes an adjective: serious.","g":"AD","a":[["serious"]],"h":["serious"]},{"i":"b1-14","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"My brother closed the fridge very ___ (quiet). He had just eaten the last pudding.","f":"\"Closed\" is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: quietly.","g":"AD","a":[["quietly"]],"h":["quietly"]},{"i":"b1-15","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"The singer ___ (proud) showed us her new guitar and then dropped it.","f":"\"Showed\" is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: proudly.","g":"AD","a":[["proudly"]],"h":["proudly"]},{"i":"b1-16","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"Your handwriting is ___ (beautiful). Mine looks like a spider fell into the ink.","f":"After \"is\" you need an adjective. It describes the handwriting: beautiful.","g":"AD","a":[["beautiful"]],"h":["beautiful"]},{"i":"b1-17","s":"b1","t":"fix","x":"Our neighbour plays the trumpet *bad*, and he plays it every evening.","f":"\"Plays\" is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: badly.","g":"AD","a":[["badly"]],"h":["badly"]},{"i":"b1-18","s":"b1","t":"fix","x":"Amara spoke *clearly*, so even the people at the back understood her.","f":"\"Spoke\" is a verb, so the adverb \"clearly\" is correct.","g":"AD","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"b2-01","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"Lena is a good dancer. She dances really ___.","f":"The adverb of \"good\" is \"well\".","g":"LY","c":"well","w":["good","goodly"]},{"i":"b2-02","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"Slow down! You are driving too ___.","f":"\"Fast\" is an adjective and an adverb. There is no \"fastly\".","g":"LY","c":"fast","w":["fastly","fastest"]},{"i":"b2-03","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"We worked ___ all weekend, and the teacher still gave the project a three.","f":"\"Hard\" stays the same as an adverb: we worked hard.","g":"LY","c":"hard","w":["hardly","more hard"]},{"i":"b2-04","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"The bus arrived ___ again, so I missed the first lesson. What a shame.","f":"\"Late\" stays the same as an adverb: the bus arrived late.","g":"LY","c":"late","w":["lately"]},{"i":"b2-05","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"He ___ opened the present and found socks. Again.","f":"\"Opened\" is a verb, and \"happy\" ends in -y, so the adverb is \"happily\".","g":"LY","c":"happily","w":["happyly","happy"]},{"i":"b2-06","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"Your friend got a good mark. Which sentence is correct?","f":"\"Did\" is a verb, so you need the adverb of \"good\": well.","g":"LY","c":"She did well in the test.","w":["She did good in the test.","She did goodly in the test."]},{"i":"b2-07","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"The door opens ___ when you walk towards it. My little brother still thinks it is magic.","f":"\"Automatic\" ends in -ic, so the adverb is \"automatically\".","g":"LY","c":"automatically","w":["automaticly","automatic"]},{"i":"b2-08","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"My little brother chews so ___ that I have to leave the room.","f":"\"Noisy\" ends in -y, so the adverb is \"noisily\".","g":"LY","c":"noisily","w":["noisy","noisely"]},{"i":"b2-09","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"Kian is a ___ runner, but he swims ___.","f":"\"Runner\" is a noun: fast. \"Swims\" is a verb, so you need the adverb: badly.","g":"LY","c":"fast … badly","w":["fastly … bad","fast … bad"]},{"i":"b2-10","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"You speak English very ___ (good). Where did you learn it?","f":"The adverb of \"good\" is \"well\".","g":"LY","a":[["well"]],"h":["well"]},{"i":"b2-11","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"My cat ___ (angry) pushed my glass off the table because dinner was four minutes late.","f":"\"Angry\" ends in -y, so the adverb is \"angrily\".","g":"LY","a":[["angrily"]],"h":["angrily"]},{"i":"b2-12","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"My dad danced at the wedding. He danced ___ (terrible), and somebody filmed it.","f":"\"Terrible\" ends in -le, so the adverb is \"terribly\".","g":"LY","a":[["terribly"]],"h":["terribly"]},{"i":"b2-13","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"She can run really ___ (fast). Nobody in our year has ever caught her.","f":"\"Fast\" stays the same as an adverb. There is no \"fastly\".","g":"LY","a":[["fast"]],"h":["fast"]},{"i":"b2-14","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"We sat ___ (comfortable) on the sofa and watched four episodes in a row.","f":"\"Comfortable\" ends in -le, so the adverb is \"comfortably\".","g":"LY","a":[["comfortably"]],"h":["comfortably"]},{"i":"b2-15","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"He trains ___ (hard) every day, and he still loses to his little sister.","f":"\"Hard\" stays the same as an adverb: he trains hard.","g":"LY","a":[["hard"]],"h":["hard"]},{"i":"b2-16","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"The ending changed ___ (dramatic) in the last five minutes.","f":"\"Dramatic\" ends in -ic, so the adverb is \"dramatically\".","g":"LY","a":[["dramatically"]],"h":["dramatically"]},{"i":"b2-17","s":"b2","t":"fix","x":"My brother cooks really *good*. Sadly, he only does it when he is hungry himself.","f":"\"Cooks\" is a verb, so you need the adverb of \"good\": well.","g":"LY","a":[["well"]],"h":["well"]},{"i":"b2-18","s":"b2","t":"fix","x":"Our dog eats *fast*, so nobody has ever seen what is in his bowl.","f":"\"Fast\" is an adjective and an adverb, so \"eats fast\" is correct.","g":"LY","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"bc-01","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"The children were ___ for once, so we could hear the film.","f":"After \"were\" you need an adjective: quiet.","g":"AD","c":"quiet","w":["quietly","quietness"]},{"i":"bc-02","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"He ___ ate the last slice while nobody was looking.","f":"\"Ate\" is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: quickly.","g":"AD","c":"quickly","w":["quick","quickness"]},{"i":"bc-03","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"Emre speaks three languages ___, and he is only sixteen.","f":"\"Speaks\" is a verb, so you need the adverb of \"good\": well.","g":"LY","c":"well","w":["good","goodly"]},{"i":"bc-04","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"You are talking about a film. Which sentence is correct?","f":"\"Ended\" is a verb, and the adverb of \"happy\" is \"happily\".","g":"LY","c":"The film ended happily.","w":["The film ended happy.","The film ended happyly."]},{"i":"bc-05","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"My mum is a ___ driver. She parks ___ and never hits anything.","f":"\"Driver\" is a noun: safe. \"Parks\" is a verb: carefully.","g":"AD","c":"safe … carefully","w":["safely … careful","safe … careful"]},{"i":"bc-06","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"The instructions were ___ (simple), but I still built the shelf upside down.","f":"After \"were\" you need an adjective. It describes the instructions: simple.","g":"AD","a":[["simple"]],"h":["simple"]},{"i":"bc-07","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"He ___ (brave) opened the door, and it was only the cat.","f":"\"Opened\" is a verb, and a verb takes an adverb: bravely.","g":"AD","a":[["bravely"]],"h":["bravely"]},{"i":"bc-08","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"She worked ___ (hard) for that grade, so don't call it luck.","f":"\"Hard\" stays the same as an adverb: she worked hard.","g":"LY","a":[["hard"]],"h":["hard"]},{"i":"bc-09","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"We won ___ (easy). The other team had only six players.","f":"\"Easy\" ends in -y, so the adverb is \"easily\".","g":"LY","a":[["easily"]],"h":["easily"]},{"i":"bc-10","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"My phone is ___ (slow) today. It needs ten seconds to open the camera.","f":"After \"is\" you need an adjective. It describes the phone: slow.","g":"AD","a":[["slow"]],"h":["slow"]},{"i":"bc-11","s":"bc","t":"fix","x":"Don't worry, I can cook quite *good*. Nobody has died so far.","f":"\"Cook\" is a verb, so you need the adverb of \"good\": well.","g":"LY","a":[["well"]],"h":["well"]},{"i":"bc-12","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"Noor is a ___ (good) singer, and she plays the guitar ___ (good) too.","f":"\"Singer\" is a noun: good. \"Plays\" is a verb, so you need the adverb: well.","g":"LY","a":[["good"],["well"]],"h":["good","well"]},{"i":"k1-01","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"My new phone is ___ than the old one, and it no longer fits in my pocket.","f":"\"Big\" is a short adjective: big → bigger.","g":"CA","c":"bigger","w":["more big","biger"]},{"i":"k1-02","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"This is the ___ book I have ever read. I fell asleep on page three.","f":"\"Boring\" is a long adjective, and \"the … I have ever read\" needs the superlative: most boring.","g":"CA","c":"most boring","w":["boringest","more boring"]},{"i":"k1-03","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"Maths is ___ than history for me. Numbers don't ask for my opinion.","f":"\"Easy\" is short and ends in -y: easy → easier.","g":"CA","c":"easier","w":["more easy","easyer"]},{"i":"k1-04","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"I am not as ___ as my brother, but I can still beat him at basketball.","f":"After \"as … as\" the adjective keeps its base form: as tall as.","g":"CA","c":"tall","w":["taller","tallest"]},{"i":"k1-05","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"Tickets for the festival are more expensive ___ last year.","f":"After a comparative you use \"than\". \"As\" is the German trap.","g":"CA","c":"than","w":["as","then"]},{"i":"k1-06","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"You warn a friend who is new in town. Which sentence is correct?","f":"\"Dangerous\" is a long adjective, so the superlative is \"the most dangerous\".","g":"CA","c":"This is the most dangerous road in town.","w":["This is the dangerousest road in town.","This is the more dangerous road in town."]},{"i":"k1-07","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"February is the ___ month of the year.","f":"\"Short\" is a short adjective, and \"the … of the year\" needs the superlative: shortest.","g":"CA","c":"shortest","w":["most short","shorter"]},{"i":"k1-08","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"My sister's room is ___ than mine, and she still wants my desk.","f":"\"Nice\" is a short adjective: nice → nicer.","g":"CA","c":"nicer","w":["more nice","niceer"]},{"i":"k1-09","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"The last level is ___ than the rest of the game put together.","f":"\"Difficult\" is a long adjective: more difficult.","g":"CA","c":"more difficult","w":["difficulter","most difficult"]},{"i":"k1-10","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"The blue whale is the ___ (big) animal on Earth, and it lives on tiny krill.","f":"\"Big\" is a short adjective, and \"the … on Earth\" needs the superlative: biggest.","g":"CA","a":[["biggest"]],"h":["biggest"]},{"i":"k1-11","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"Your little brother is ___ (funny) than you. Sorry.","f":"\"Funny\" is short and ends in -y: funny → funnier.","g":"CA","a":[["funnier"]],"h":["funnier"]},{"i":"k1-12","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"The sequel was ___ (interesting) than the first film, which never happens.","f":"\"Interesting\" is a long adjective: more interesting.","g":"CA","a":[["more interesting"]],"h":["more interesting"]},{"i":"k1-13","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"This is the ___ (cheap) kebab in our street, and you can taste it.","f":"\"Cheap\" is a short adjective, and \"the … in our street\" needs the superlative: cheapest.","g":"CA","a":[["cheapest"]],"h":["cheapest"]},{"i":"k1-14","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"Who is the ___ (famous) person you have ever met? A man from a yoghurt advert counts.","f":"\"Famous\" is a long adjective, and \"the … you have ever met\" needs the superlative: most famous.","g":"CA","a":[["most famous"]],"h":["most famous"]},{"i":"k1-15","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"My bag is ___ (heavy) than yours because I carry all my books and three old sandwiches.","f":"\"Heavy\" is short and ends in -y: heavy → heavier.","g":"CA","a":[["heavier"]],"h":["heavier"]},{"i":"k1-16","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"Mondays are ___ (long) than any other day. That is how it feels, anyway.","f":"\"Long\" is a short adjective: long → longer.","g":"CA","a":[["longer"]],"h":["longer"]},{"i":"k1-17","s":"k1","t":"fix","x":"My little brother is already taller *as* me.","f":"After a comparative you use \"than\", not \"as\".","g":"CA","a":[["than"]],"h":["than"]},{"i":"k1-18","s":"k1","t":"fix","x":"This is the *most beautiful* beach I have ever seen.","f":"\"Beautiful\" is a long adjective, so \"most beautiful\" is correct.","g":"CA","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"k2-01","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Your pasta is good, but my grandma's is ___.","f":"\"Good\" is irregular: good → better → best.","g":"IR","c":"better","w":["gooder","more good"]},{"i":"k2-02","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"That was the ___ goal of the whole season. The ball went in off his knee.","f":"\"Bad\" is irregular, and \"the … of the season\" needs the superlative: worst.","g":"IR","c":"worst","w":["baddest","worse"]},{"i":"k2-03","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Can you explain it ___? I still don't get it.","f":"Adverbs with -ly take \"more\": more clearly.","g":"CV","c":"more clearly","w":["clearlier","most clearly"]},{"i":"k2-04","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"She trains ___ than anyone else in the team, and it shows.","f":"\"Hard\" has no -ly, so the comparative is \"harder\".","g":"CV","c":"harder","w":["more hard","more hardly"]},{"i":"k2-05","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"My marks are getting ___ every year. My parents have stopped asking.","f":"\"Bad\" is irregular: bad → worse → worst.","g":"IR","c":"worse","w":["worser","more bad"]},{"i":"k2-06","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"You asked a stranger for the way. Which sentence is correct?","f":"\"Answered\" needs an adverb, and adverbs with -ly take \"more\": more politely.","g":"CV","c":"She answered more politely than I expected.","w":["She answered politelier than I expected.","She answered more polite than I expected."]},{"i":"k2-07","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Mika plays the guitar ___ than me, but I am louder.","f":"The comparative of \"well\" is \"better\".","g":"CV","c":"better","w":["weller","more well"]},{"i":"k2-08","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Our school is ___ from the station than the map says. Wear good shoes.","f":"\"Far\" is irregular: far → further → furthest.","g":"IR","c":"further","w":["farer","more far"]},{"i":"k2-09","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Of all my friends, Amara runs the ___.","f":"\"Fast\" has no -ly, so the superlative is \"fastest\".","g":"CV","c":"fastest","w":["most fast","most fastly"]},{"i":"k2-10","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"This is the ___ (good) idea you have had all year. Write it down.","f":"\"Good\" is irregular: good → better → best.","g":"IR","a":[["best"]],"h":["best"]},{"i":"k2-11","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"My headache is ___ (bad) than it was this morning. I blame the maths test.","f":"\"Bad\" is irregular: bad → worse → worst.","g":"IR","a":[["worse"]],"h":["worse"]},{"i":"k2-12","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"She speaks French ___ (fluent) than her teacher, which makes lessons a bit awkward.","f":"\"Speaks\" needs an adverb, and adverbs with -ly take \"more\": more fluently.","g":"CV","a":[["more fluently"]],"h":["more fluently"]},{"i":"k2-13","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"In 2009 Usain Bolt ran ___ (fast) than anyone before him: 100 metres in 9.58 seconds.","f":"\"Fast\" has no -ly, so the comparative is \"faster\".","g":"CV","a":[["faster"]],"h":["faster"]},{"i":"k2-14","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"Who sings ___ (bad), you or your dad? I have heard both, and it is close.","f":"The comparative of \"badly\" is \"worse\".","g":"CV","a":[["worse"]],"h":["worse"]},{"i":"k2-15","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"We walked ___ (far) than we had planned, and the last bus had already left.","f":"\"Far\" is irregular: far → further → furthest.","g":"IR","a":[["farther","further"]],"h":["further"]},{"i":"k2-16","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"Of everyone in the group, Jonas explained it the ___ (good).","f":"The superlative of \"well\" is \"best\".","g":"CV","a":[["best"]],"h":["best"]},{"i":"k2-17","s":"k2","t":"fix","x":"My cooking is *more bad* than yours, and you once burned water.","f":"\"Bad\" is irregular: bad → worse → worst.","g":"IR","a":[["worse"]],"h":["worse"]},{"i":"k2-18","s":"k2","t":"fix","x":"Could you talk *more quietly*? Some of us are trying to sleep.","f":"Adverbs with -ly take \"more\", so \"more quietly\" is correct.","g":"CV","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"kc-01","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"The blue trainers are ___ than the white ones, but they look much better.","f":"\"Cheap\" is a short adjective: cheap → cheaper.","g":"CA","c":"cheaper","w":["more cheap","cheapest"]},{"i":"kc-02","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"That was the ___ day of my life. First the bus, then the test, then the rain.","f":"\"Bad\" is irregular: bad → worse → worst.","g":"IR","c":"worst","w":["baddest","most bad"]},{"i":"kc-03","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"Nobody in our class writes ___ than Noor. Her notes look printed.","f":"\"Writes\" needs an adverb, and adverbs with -ly take \"more\": more beautifully.","g":"CV","c":"more beautifully","w":["beautifullier","more beautiful"]},{"i":"kc-04","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"You and your cousin were born in the same year. Which sentence is correct?","f":"After \"as … as\" the adjective keeps its base form.","g":"CA","c":"My cousin is as old as me.","w":["My cousin is as older as me.","My cousin is as old than me."]},{"i":"kc-05","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"The film is good, but the book is even ___.","f":"\"Good\" is irregular: good → better → best.","g":"IR","c":"better","w":["more good","gooder"]},{"i":"kc-06","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"The cheetah is the ___ (fast) land animal, but it gets tired after a few hundred metres.","f":"\"Fast\" is a short adjective, and \"the … land animal\" needs the superlative: fastest.","g":"CA","a":[["fastest"]],"h":["fastest"]},{"i":"kc-07","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"That is the ___ (expensive) sandwich I have ever bought. It had better be amazing.","f":"\"Expensive\" is a long adjective, and \"the … I have ever bought\" needs the superlative.","g":"CA","a":[["most expensive"]],"h":["most expensive"]},{"i":"kc-08","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"You are ___ (lucky) than me. I have never won anything, not even a pen.","f":"\"Lucky\" is short and ends in -y: lucky → luckier.","g":"CA","a":[["luckier"]],"h":["luckier"]},{"i":"kc-09","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"Our team played ___ (bad) than last week, and last week we lost 0–5.","f":"The comparative of \"badly\" is \"worse\".","g":"CV","a":[["worse"]],"h":["worse"]},{"i":"kc-10","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"Please read the instructions ___ (careful) than last time. We still have a hole in the wall.","f":"Adverbs with -ly take \"more\": more carefully.","g":"CV","a":[["more carefully"]],"h":["more carefully"]},{"i":"kc-11","s":"kc","t":"fix","x":"This song is *more good* than their last one.","f":"\"Good\" is irregular: good → better → best.","g":"IR","a":[["better"]],"h":["better"]},{"i":"kc-12","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"The second half was ___ (exciting) than the first, and the last ten minutes were the ___ (good) of the whole match.","f":"\"Exciting\" is a long adjective: more exciting. \"Good\" is irregular: the best.","g":"CA","a":[["more exciting"],["best"]],"h":["more exciting","best"]},{"i":"p1-01","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"This pizza smells ___. Is that pineapple?","f":"After \"smells\" you need an adjective. It describes the pizza: strange.","g":"LV","c":"strange","w":["strangely","strangeness"]},{"i":"p1-02","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"You sound ___. Did you get the job?","f":"After \"sound\" you need an adjective. It describes \"you\": happy.","g":"LV","c":"happy","w":["happily","happiness"]},{"i":"p1-03","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"The lake was ___ warm, so we stayed in for an hour.","f":"\"Warm\" is an adjective, and the word that describes an adjective is an adverb: surprisingly warm.","g":"AV","c":"surprisingly","w":["surprising","surprise"]},{"i":"p1-04","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"She looked ___ at the price and put the jacket back.","f":"\"Looked at\" is an action here, so you need an adverb: nervously.","g":"LV","c":"nervously","w":["nervous","nerves"]},{"i":"p1-05","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"My little brother is ___ good at chess. He beat my dad in ten minutes.","f":"\"Good\" is an adjective, and the word that describes an adjective is an adverb: annoyingly good.","g":"AV","c":"annoyingly","w":["annoying","annoyed"]},{"i":"p1-06","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"A friend plays you a new song, and you like it. Which sentence is correct?","f":"After \"sounds\" you need an adjective: great.","g":"LV","c":"Your new song sounds great.","w":["Your new song sounds greatly.","Your new song sounds well."]},{"i":"p1-07","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"I felt ___ after the third burger. I regret nothing.","f":"After \"felt\" you need an adjective. It describes \"I\": terrible.","g":"LV","c":"terrible","w":["terribly","terror"]},{"i":"p1-08","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"You look ___ tired. Did you sleep at all?","f":"\"Tired\" is an adjective, and the word that describes an adjective is an adverb: really tired.","g":"AV","c":"really","w":["real","reality"]},{"i":"p1-09","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"A dog has found something interesting. Which sentence is correct?","f":"Here \"smelled\" is an action: the dog did something. So you need the adverb, and it comes after the object.","g":"LV","c":"The dog smelled the bag carefully.","w":["The dog smelled the bag careful.","The dog smelled carefully the bag."]},{"i":"p1-10","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"Your plan sounds ___ (perfect). What could possibly go wrong?","f":"After \"sounds\" you need an adjective. It describes the plan: perfect.","g":"LV","a":[["perfect"]],"h":["perfect"]},{"i":"p1-11","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"The cake looks ___ (amazing), but it tastes ___ (terrible).","f":"After \"looks\" and \"tastes\" you need adjectives. They describe the cake.","g":"LV","a":[["amazing"],["terrible"]],"h":["amazing","terrible"]},{"i":"p1-12","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"I am ___ (absolute) sure that I locked the door. Fairly sure. Maybe.","f":"\"Sure\" is an adjective, and the word that describes an adjective is an adverb: absolutely sure.","g":"AV","a":[["absolutely"]],"h":["absolutely"]},{"i":"p1-13","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"He looked ___ (careful) at the screen and then deleted the whole chat.","f":"\"Looked at\" is an action here, so you need an adverb: carefully.","g":"LV","a":[["carefully"]],"h":["carefully"]},{"i":"p1-14","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"My hands feel ___ (cold). Who had the idea of a picnic in November?","f":"After \"feel\" you need an adjective. It describes the hands: cold.","g":"LV","a":[["cold"]],"h":["cold"]},{"i":"p1-15","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"The concert was ___ (incredible) loud. My ears are still ringing.","f":"\"Loud\" is an adjective, and the word that describes an adjective is an adverb: incredibly loud.","g":"AV","a":[["incredibly"]],"h":["incredibly"]},{"i":"p1-16","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"You seem ___ (nervous). Is it the test, or is it me?","f":"After \"seem\" you need an adjective. It describes \"you\": nervous.","g":"LV","a":[["nervous"]],"h":["nervous"]},{"i":"p1-17","s":"p1","t":"fix","x":"This milk smells *badly*. How long has it been in your bag?","f":"After \"smells\" you need an adjective. It describes the milk: bad.","g":"LV","a":[["bad"]],"h":["bad"]},{"i":"p1-18","s":"p1","t":"fix","x":"It was an *unusually* quiet afternoon. Then my cousins arrived.","f":"\"Quiet\" is an adjective, so the adverb \"unusually\" in front of it is correct.","g":"AV","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"p2-01","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"I ___ know him. We have talked twice, and both times it was about the weather.","f":"\"Hardly\" means \"almost not\": I hardly know him.","g":"HL","c":"hardly","w":["hard","harder"]},{"i":"p2-02","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"She studied ___ for the exam and got the best mark in the class.","f":"\"Hard\" means \"with a lot of effort\". \"Hardly\" would mean \"almost not\".","g":"HL","c":"hard","w":["hardly"]},{"i":"p2-03","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"I have been really tired ___. Maybe I should go to bed before two.","f":"\"Lately\" means \"in the last few weeks\".","g":"HL","c":"lately","w":["late","later"]},{"i":"p2-04","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"Sorry, I got up ___ and missed the bus.","f":"\"Late\" means \"not on time\". \"Lately\" would mean \"in the last few weeks\".","g":"HL","c":"late","w":["lately"]},{"i":"p2-05","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence means that Ben did almost no work?","f":"\"Hardly\" means \"almost not\". \"Worked hard\" means the opposite.","g":"HL","c":"Ben hardly worked.","w":["Ben worked hard."]},{"i":"p2-06","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"It is so loud in here that I can ___ hear you.","f":"\"Hardly\" means \"almost not\": I can hardly hear you.","g":"HL","c":"hardly","w":["hard","harder"]},{"i":"p2-07","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"Have you watched anything good ___? I need a new series.","f":"\"Lately\" means \"in the last few weeks\", and it often comes with the present perfect.","g":"HL","c":"lately","w":["late","lastly"]},{"i":"p2-08","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"I have ___ slept ___, so please don't talk to me before ten.","f":"\"Hardly\" means \"almost not\", and \"lately\" means \"in the last few weeks\".","g":"HL","c":"hardly … lately","w":["hard … late","hard … lately"]},{"i":"p2-09","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"He hit the ball so ___ that it flew over the fence and into the neighbour's pool.","f":"\"Hard\" means \"with a lot of force\". \"Hardly\" would mean \"almost not\".","g":"HL","c":"hard","w":["hardly","hardness"]},{"i":"p2-10","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"There was ___ (hard) any food left when we arrived. Just one sad carrot.","f":"\"Hardly any\" means \"almost no\".","g":"HL","a":[["hardly"]],"h":["hardly"]},{"i":"p2-11","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"If you work ___ (hard), you can finish it tonight.","f":"\"Hard\" means \"with a lot of effort\", and it has no -ly.","g":"HL","a":[["hard"]],"h":["hard"]},{"i":"p2-12","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"My sister has been in a strange mood ___ (late). She even tidied her room.","f":"\"Lately\" means \"in the last few weeks\".","g":"HL","a":[["lately"]],"h":["lately"]},{"i":"p2-13","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"The film started ___ (late) because the projector was broken.","f":"\"Late\" means \"not on time\", and it has no -ly.","g":"HL","a":[["late"]],"h":["late"]},{"i":"p2-14","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"I could ___ (hard) believe my eyes. My dad was dancing.","f":"\"Hardly\" means \"almost not\": I could hardly believe it.","g":"HL","a":[["hardly"]],"h":["hardly"]},{"i":"p2-15","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"I have not been to the gym ___ (late). To be honest, I have never been to the gym.","f":"\"Lately\" means \"in the last few weeks\".","g":"HL","a":[["lately"]],"h":["lately"]},{"i":"p2-16","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"It is raining ___ (hard), so take the big umbrella.","f":"\"Hard\" means \"with a lot of force\", and it has no -ly.","g":"HL","a":[["hard"]],"h":["hard"]},{"i":"p2-17","s":"p2","t":"fix","x":"We tried *hardly*, but the other team was simply better.","f":"\"Hard\" means \"with a lot of effort\". \"Hardly\" means \"almost not\".","g":"HL","a":[["hard"]],"h":["hard"]},{"i":"p2-18","s":"p2","t":"fix","x":"He always comes home *late* on Fridays.","f":"\"Late\" means \"not on time\", so it is correct here.","g":"HL","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"pc-01","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"That jacket looks ___ on you. Is it new?","f":"After \"looks\" you need an adjective. It describes the jacket: good.","g":"LV","c":"good","w":["well","goodly"]},{"i":"pc-02","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"I ___ recognised her with the new haircut.","f":"\"Hardly\" means \"almost not\": I hardly recognised her.","g":"HL","c":"hardly","w":["hard","lately"]},{"i":"pc-03","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"The instructions were ___ useless, so we just pressed every button.","f":"\"Useless\" is an adjective, and the word that describes an adjective is an adverb: completely useless.","g":"AV","c":"completely","w":["complete","completion"]},{"i":"pc-04","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"You try the coffee in the school canteen. Which sentence is correct?","f":"After \"tastes\" you need an adjective: awful.","g":"LV","c":"This coffee tastes awful.","w":["This coffee tastes awfully.","This coffee awful tastes."]},{"i":"pc-05","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"I have been working really ___ ___, so I need the weekend.","f":"\"Hard\" means \"with a lot of effort\", and \"lately\" means \"in the last few weeks\".","g":"HL","c":"hard … lately","w":["hardly … late","hardly … lately"]},{"i":"pc-06","s":"pc","t":"fix","x":"The soup smells *wonderfully*. What is in it?","f":"After \"smells\" you need an adjective: wonderful.","g":"LV","a":[["wonderful"]],"h":["wonderful"]},{"i":"pc-07","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"Your voice sounds ___ (different) on the phone. I thought you were your mum.","f":"After \"sounds\" you need an adjective. It describes the voice: different.","g":"LV","a":[["different"]],"h":["different"]},{"i":"pc-08","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"I am ___ (terrible) sorry about your bike. I will pay for the wheel.","f":"\"Sorry\" is an adjective, and the word that describes an adjective is an adverb: terribly sorry.","g":"AV","a":[["terribly"]],"h":["terribly"]},{"i":"pc-09","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"We ___ (hard) see each other these days. She moved to Hamburg in March.","f":"\"Hardly\" means \"almost not\": we hardly see each other.","g":"HL","a":[["hardly"]],"h":["hardly"]},{"i":"pc-10","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"You have been very quiet ___ (late). Is everything OK?","f":"\"Lately\" means \"in the last few weeks\".","g":"HL","a":[["lately"]],"h":["lately"]},{"i":"pc-11","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"He looked ___ (angry) at the referee and walked off the pitch.","f":"\"Looked at\" is an action here, so you need an adverb: angrily.","g":"LV","a":[["angrily"]],"h":["angrily"]},{"i":"pc-12","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"The test looked ___ (easy), but it was ___ (surprising) hard.","f":"After \"looked\" you need an adjective: easy. \"Hard\" is an adjective here, so the word before it is an adverb: surprisingly.","g":"LV","a":[["easy"],["surprisingly"]],"h":["easy","surprisingly"]}]});
